{"game": "space-marine-2011", "language": "english", "appid": 55150, "month": "2013-10", "window": 1, "start_date": 1380585600, "end_date": 1383263999, "month_true_total": 17, "quota": 17, "returned": 17, "pulled_at": "2026-10-09 17:48:03 UTC", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "7517905", "author": {"steamid": "76561198008792493", "personaname": "Atticus", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198008792493/", "num_games_owned": 2482, "num_reviews": 29, "playtime_forever": 477, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 477, "last_played": 1383117891, "avatar": "55a5b702c50ad27014ad848ba55f78c51a25101d"}, "language": "english", "review": "Combat is brutal and pretty fun, espeically the melee + jetpack moments which are glorious, it helps you get through the first 4-5 hours of generic story telling. The story finally gets somewhat interesting for your last little bit of gameplay. It's a bit above average game with some good fighting, but no variety and slow story make it a bit of grind to get to the ending.", "timestamp_created": 1383118685, "timestamp_updated": 1383118685, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": false, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1315281600", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "7492036", "author": {"steamid": "76561197998703252", "personaname": "scrypt", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/neverhouse/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 23, "playtime_forever": 921, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 757, "last_played": 1619494383, "avatar": "a0e9851f8bb374a032caa3f2d93293dc720cb64b"}, "language": "english", "review": "The thing that keeps me coming back to Space Marine is the attention to detail in scale and space that Relic put into this game. The combat is intense and gratuitous, and the story and voice acting are everything you would want in a grand space opera, but it's the environment that I can't get enough of. Never has such linear game-play felt so free and open.", "timestamp_created": 1382861347, "timestamp_updated": 1382861347, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 2, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.537537515163421631", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1315281600", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "7486372", "author": {"steamid": "76561198085368350", "personaname": "MosinBoi_2007", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/pique311/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 7, "playtime_forever": 3446, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 2804, "last_played": 1710094127, "avatar": "170011a9d95b57dfbbac6db6b929c46dff09b802"}, "language": "english", "review": "I am an experienced Warhammer 40k player (I mean the real board game), and all I can say is whenever I play this game, I ♥♥♥♥♥♥♥ feel like a real Ultramarine (my army), very enjoyable when you crush orks' craniums.\n(Forget about the online now, I have played it like two years ago and not much people was playing it but it was ok. If you come to find a game with more people you can have a good time but I suggest to play the campaing only)", "timestamp_created": 1382809743, "timestamp_updated": 1452126027, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.476190477609634399", "comment_count": 1, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1315281600", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "7456143", "author": {"steamid": "76561198007402220", "personaname": "ayy LMAO", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url"